# Weapon authoring binaries are local-only: the .bbmodel sources, the baked
# legacy model trees and the sound samples live in the author's library and are
# copied into this resource tree for local builds. A fresh clone ships the
# PLACEHOLDER.md notes instead, and the module still enables — the guns just
# render on their vanilla carrier and fire silently.
src/main/resources/defaults/models/gun/*.bbmodel
src/main/resources/defaults/models/gun/*.png
src/main/resources/defaults/models/gun/*.meta.json
src/main/resources/defaults/sounds/mineplusgun/*.ogg

# The shipped gun tree is content, not authoring scratch: every model JSON and
# every per-gun sprite under defaults/guns/<id>/ belongs in the jar, so undo
# the repository-wide image exclusions for it.
!src/main/resources/defaults/guns/**/*.json
!src/main/resources/defaults/guns/**/*.png

# The retired Western frame import (superseded by defaults/guns/) is excluded
# from the jar by build.gradle; keep it out of the working tree's status too.
src/main/resources/defaults/frames/
